Vulnerability Category

Security Misconfiguration / Code Integrity

Description

It was observed that application DLL files are not digitally signed, preventing validation of their integrity. These DLLs are loaded dynamically by the Excel add-in from shared locations. Lack of code signing allows unauthorized modification without detection. This introduces risk of malicious code execution.

Impact
Attackers can replace DLLs with malicious code
Leads to execution of unauthorized code within Excel environment
Potential full system compromise
Recommendations

It is recommended to digitally sign all DLLs using trusted code-signing certificates. Enforce integrity checks before loading binaries in the application. Restrict write access to DLL directories and monitor for unauthorized changes. Implement application whitelisting to prevent execution of untrusted binaries.

