🔴 7. Insecure LDAP Communication (Non-LDAPS)
Risk

High

CVSS 3.1

8.2 (High)

Vulnerability Category

Insecure Communication

Description

It was observed that LDAP communication is configured without using secure protocols such as LDAPS. Communication occurs over standard LDAP, which transmits data in plaintext. Sensitive credentials are exposed during transmission. This increases risk of interception attacks.

Impact
Credentials can be intercepted over the network
Enables man-in-the-middle attacks
Unauthorized access to directory services
Recommendations

It is recommended to enforce LDAPS (port 636) with TLS encryption for all LDAP communications. Ensure certificate validation is properly implemented in the application. Disable insecure LDAP (port 389) where possible. Monitor and secure network traffic carrying authentication data.

References

https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/ad-ds/plan/security-best-practices/ldap-over-ssl-ldaps

